sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant W as WebhookController
    participant K as Kafka (meeting.events)
    participant MC as MeetingEventConsumer
    participant TS as TranscriptService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant R as Reader (GET)

    Note over C,DB: Edge case — out-of-order delivery (seq 3, 1, 2). Order is a read-time concern.

    C->>W: POST transcript seq=3
    W->>K: publish
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>TS: handleTranscript
    TS->>DB: insert segment seq=3

    C->>W: POST transcript seq=1
    W->>K: publish
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>TS: handleTranscript
    TS->>DB: insert segment seq=1

    C->>W: POST transcript seq=2
    W->>K: publish
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>TS: handleTranscript
    TS->>DB: insert segment seq=2

    Note over R,DB: Reconstruction / read always ORDER BY sequenceNumber
    R->>DB: findBySessionIdOrderBySequenceNumberAsc
    DB-->>R: segments [1, 2, 3]
